  </title>
  <description akvo:type="6" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The incorporation of gender measures in the Peace Agreement has been the result of the incidence of women in Colombia. However, the implementation of these measures is low, a situation that, together with a culture based on patriarchal values, social, economic and political inequalities for reasons of gender and different forms of violence against women, violate the exercise of human rights, a sustainable and inclusive development and democracy.
In this context, the Mujeres que Inciden en la Paz program seeks to contribute to a lasting peace process with gender justice in Colombia, in which women and girls have the same rights and opportunities as men and boys, creating conditions conducive to strengthening the participation, influence and leadership of women and their organizations in peacebuilding spaces at the local, territorial and national levels.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description akvo:type="5" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This program seeks to contribute to a lasting peace process with gender justice in Colombia, in which women and girls have the same rights and opportunities as men and boys. It is implemented by a Consortium made up of three Colombian organizations and two Dutch organizations, one of them is ICCO Cooperation, as leader of the Program.</narrative>
  </description>
